content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Employment Search": {
      "objects": [
        "Applicant",
        "CV",
        "Application",
        "Submission Status",
        "Career Guidance Meeting"
      ]
    },
    "Mediation": {
      "objects": [
        "Agent",
        "Candidate Recommendation",
        "Application",
        "Interview",
        "Applicant",
        "Employer",
        "Outcome",
        "Interview Feedback",
        "Employment Agency",
        "Candidate Request"
      ]
    },
    "Recruitment": {
      "objects": [
        "Employer",
        "Candidate Request",
        "Job Requirements",
        "Candidate Feedback"
      ]
    },
    "subdomain connections": [
      "Employment Search--Mediation",
      "Recruitment--Mediation"
    ]
  }
}
```
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Applicant",
      "description": "A person seeking employment through the agency, often represented by their CV.",
      "attributes": [
        "CV"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "CV",
      "description": "A document that captures an applicant’s skills, education, and work experience."
    },
    {
      "name": "Application",
      "description": "A formal submission by an applicant for a job, tracked by its status and linked to a CV.",
      "attributes": [
        "CV",
        "Submission Status"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Submission Status",
      "description": "The current state of an application, such as pending, accepted, or rejected."
    },
    {
      "name": "Agent",
      "description": "A staff member at the employment agency who supports applicants and employers."
    },
    {
      "name": "Career Guidance Meeting",
      "description": "A session between an agent and applicant to discuss career options and improve job readiness."
    },
    {
      "name": "Interview",
      "description": "A meeting between an applicant and employer to assess suitability, with an outcome recorded.",
      "attributes": [
        "Applicant",
        "Employer",
        "Outcome"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Employer",
      "description": "An organization seeking candidates to fill job positions."
    },
    {
      "name": "Outcome",
      "description": "The result of an interview, such as successful or unsuccessful."
    },
    {
      "name": "Interview Feedback",
      "description": "Comments provided after an interview to help the applicant improve."
    },
    {
      "name": "Candidate Recommendation",
      "description": "A suggestion made by an agent to an employer, based on an application.",
      "attributes": [
        "Application"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Candidate Request",
      "description": "A request from an employer to the agency for candidates, defined by job requirements.",
      "attributes": [
        "Job Requirements"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Job Requirements",
      "description": "The qualifications, skills, and experience needed for a role."
    },
    {
      "name": "Candidate Feedback",
      "description": "An employer’s evaluation of a candidate after review or interview."
    },
    {
      "name": "Employment Agency",
      "description": "An organization that connects applicants and employers, managing applications and candidate requests.",
      "attributes": [
        "Application",
        "Candidate Request"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
